# Codegraph (use when needed · skip when not)

Product/server = Codegraph (MCP). Tool = `codegraph_explore` **only**. **Do not call on every question.** Consider only if Index (`.codegraph/`) or MCP available.
**MCP default ≠ always call** — even if tool description says "almost any question", this Need/Skip policy applies (Priority Stack → project rules).

## Use (Need)

- Symbol / "where / who calls / call path / blast radius / how does X work"
- File name uncertain, or impact radius needed (including Mode B STEP 1 Scout)
- Before edit, need relevant symbol source + dependents at once

→ Try `codegraph_explore` before Read/Grep (once or few calls).

## Skip

- Path/file `@` or user gave exact path + context known
- Typo / single CSS fix / Fast-Track minor tweak
- Docs / Q&A / config / lockfile / non-indexed assets
- **This repo:** `.aspx`, `DBS-FFW-classicsite/2025/style.css`, `*.module.scss` visual clone, vendor `*.min.js` / UIKit / Swiper — do not index (or noise). Use `Read` / `classic-visual-parity`
- No index · MCP fail · "not indexed" → do not retry; fallback Read/Grep/Glob. May mention `codegraph init` to User — do not run yourself.

**This repo Need:** `DBS-FFW-classicsite/**/public/js/controller/*`, `DBS-FFW-classicsite/**/public/js/lib/*`, `DBS-FFW-SPFX/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` — not ASPX/CSS.

## Rules

- Do not re-verify Codegraph results with Grep unnecessarily (AST index). Read files with staleness banner only.
- Not mandatory — only when beneficial. Do not waste token/latency.
